{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "NextVision TRIP",
  "id": "nextvision_trip",
  "icd_version": "Mavlink NextVision Extension v10.10 (v110)",
  "description": "NextVision TRIP2/5/6 observation system (gimbal camera). Commands are COMMAND_LONG, reports are V2_EXTENSION whose payload is NextVision's own layout.",
  "match": { "sysid": 1, "compid": 100 },

  "annotations": [
    "Byte layouts are packed little-endian. Report payload byte 0-1 is the report type (V2_EXTENSION.message_type); ICD 'Index' n is payload byte n-6.",
    "Stated LEN is wrong in the ICD for LOS Rate (8, says 0x1A), IMU (10, says 0x40) and Fire (11, says 0x1C): the field tables are used (lengths 38, 80, 40).",
    "AR Marker (14): the ICD says up to 16 markers, but 34-byte records fit at most 7 in one MAVLink payload (2 + 12 + 7*34 = 252); max 7 is used.",
    "Snapshot (5) channel is a u8 (ICD says bytes 56-57 but LEN 0x33 implies one byte).",
    "Area Tracking (24): field table + the reference GCS (no w/h) is used, length 66 (ICD states 0x46).",
    "Variable reports: records = ceil((len - header) / record size), so MAVLink 2 trailing-zero truncation is tolerated; extra trailing bytes are ignored (ICD forward compatibility).",
    "DO_MOUNT_CONTROL NEUTRAL returns to the previous mode (ICD 2.2; 3.5.4 says GRR).",
    "Point-to-Coordinate may be entered by Set System Mode mode 12 (ICD 3.5.6; 2.2 says it cannot)."
  ],

  "enums": {
